          "worked": "Each allocation is an unordered group of three winners because the prizes are equal. Write T = Thomas, L = Leslie, A = Anthony, R = Tracie and K = Kim.\n\nWith Thomas: TLA, TLR, TLK, TAR, TAK, TRK.\n\nWithout Thomas but with Leslie: LAR, LAK, LRK.\n\nWithout Thomas or Leslie: ARK.\n\nThese are all $6+3+1=10$ allocations.",
